Z||000021||batboy||12-05-1999||01:42 AM||||That pic was in the 1st quarter 1999 edition of the FOCOA magazine. The article claims it's a Fiero. I looked at the pic in the magazine just now and it's definitely a 2 door. It looks like the whole back of the car is pushed at least a 45 degree angle away from the camera, so there's not much to see there. What's left of the hood kind of looks like a Fiero to me. Sure is hard to tell for sure though isn't it. For those of you who are wondering what we are talking about go to this page of my site.<P> <A HREF="http://sites.netscape.net/batboybain/other_fiero_pics" TARGET=_blank>http://sites.netscape.net/batboybain/other_fiero_pics</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000022||SCCA FIERO||12-05-1999||02:08 AM||||To me it looks like a Sunbird. The body looks bent and dented... a Fiero would shatter and splinter. The hood shows no headlight doors and the wheels don't have the proper offset. Grand Ams and the like have the outer lip flush with the face and the Fiero has about 1/2 an inch offset. The pillars around the windshield don't look like Fiero either.||||reg||1
Z||000023||batboy||12-05-1999||03:47 AM||||I didn't follow you about the wheels. Those are the same wheels that you see on most non-GT Fieros. I have those same wheels on all three of my Fieros. You might be right about the headlight doors though. The pic is a crappy newspaper pic, but I don't see them. The hood does look crumpled like it's steel too, don't it. Hmmmm, maybe I should take this off my site. I hate getting lied to.||||reg||1
Z||000024||RZURCTN||12-05-1999||08:22 AM||||I'll have to agree that it doesn't look like a Fiero.  It may be a 2 door, but if you look behind what's left of the door you'll see what appears to be a window.  <BR>  But I really do like the 4X4 Fiero.  I've always wanted to do that with one.  Maybe take a 4X4 S10 frame and modify it a little, and graft a fiero frame onto it.  Someday,..... someday  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  It's a really cool pic though!!||||reg||1
